3.1 Rotor-induced velocities
In general, since the mean rotor thrust—in combination with the operating condition (advance ratio, angle of attack)—provides the mean induced velocity plus its gradients longitudinally (=1/rev cosine variation) and laterally (=1/rev sine variation) as described before, the harmonic blade loading must be analyzed for the frequency range at integer harmonics above this range, i.e., from 2/rev to 6/rev, which covers the range of frequencies of interest. The limitation to the range of 2-6/rev is justified, because the higher the frequency, the smaller the wave length. Furthermore, the lift amplitudes of the higher harmonics usually are significantly smaller than those of the lower
