6 Discussion
In general, a large improvement is achieved when using the harmonic inflow model and the associated wake distortions. The cause of this improvement is identified from the wake distortions due to the dynamic part of the loading, which is most apparent when active control is applied. In these cases, a classic prescribed wake model does not change at all since the general operating condition remains unchanged. The only difference of active control cases to the baseline case without active control is due to a different blade motion which only slightly modifies the BVI zones. Yet the majority of active control effect on noise radiation is not due to a modified blade motion but is due to a modified wake geometry, which is ten times larger than the
